<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Bigerriones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aquitanian people of the high Pyrenean valleys around Tarbes, who gave their name to Bigorre.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bigerriones lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adour">Adour</a> valley and the Pyrenean foothills of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hautes-pyrenees">Hautes-Pyrénées</a>. Caesar lists them among the Aquitanian peoples who surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 56 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers. Like other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquitani">Aquitani</a> they spoke a language related to Basque, and their economy combined mountain herding with farming in the valleys.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarbes">Turba</a>, later Tarbes, within the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novempopulania">Novempopulana</a>. Their name passed to the medieval <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-bigorre">County of Bigorre</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bigerriones.jpg" alt="Bigerriones" width="320" height="274"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aquitani_tribes_map-fr.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bigerri</dd></dl></aside></div>

